Laravel's CSRF protection will block POST requests to the event endpoint by default, which is required for tracking to work [1]. You must add the event route to your CSRF exceptions in your `bootstrap/app.php` file [1]:

```php
->withMiddleware(function (Middleware $middleware) {
    $middleware->validateCsrfTokens(except: [
        'api/event', // Add this line
    ]);
})
```

If events are still not appearing, note that the Events API returns 202 Accepted even if an event is dropped, often because the `X-Forwarded-For` header contains a server IP instead of the visitor's [2]. You can debug this by adding the `X-Debug-Request: true` header to test requests to see which IP address Plausible receives [3].

